# Station installer for Windows (#2675 slice W): the counterpart of install.sh
# for the prebuilt station-server-win32-x64.zip archive.
#
# This script is a thin bootstrap. Verifying the signed release manifest
# needs Ed25519, which neither Windows PowerShell 5.1 nor PowerShell 7 offers,
# so it first finds a Node.js, then runs the installer core (a generated
# block below, bundled from packages/shared/src/installer/) with it. In order
# of preference:
#   host       a Node.js 20 or newer on PATH;
#   installed  the Node.js inside this channel's installed archive
#              (<install root>\current\runtime\node.exe), only when the
#              install root lies beneath the user profile and is restricted
#              to this user alone, as the installer leaves it; copied to a
#              private temporary directory first, since its version can be
#              removed while this script runs;
#   pinned     the official Node.js zip pinned below by sha256, downloaded and
#              used only to verify and extract, never to run Station.
#
# Configuration comes from the environment, exactly as for install.sh (see
# docs/guides/release-channel-ports.md), so both `irm <url> | iex` and
# `powershell -File install.ps1 install` work. It installs (or upgrades) a
# channel from a signed public manifest, stages a version for a service
# (STATION_INSTALL_STAGE_ONLY=1), and uninstalls (`-File install.ps1
# uninstall [-PurgeData]`). Switching a version under a Windows Station
# service arrives with slice W3 of #2675; until then such an install is
# refused.
#
# Runs on Windows PowerShell 5.1 and PowerShell 7. Every path runs inside
# the script block below, so `iex` parses the whole script before running
# any of it, and a failure never exits the caller's interactive session.

$stationInstallStatus = & {
  Set-StrictMode -Version 2.0
  $ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
  $ProgressPreference = 'SilentlyContinue'

# BEGIN GENERATED INSTALLABLE CHANNELS
# Generated by scripts/install-script-generated.mjs from config/channel-ports.json. Do not edit by hand.
$InstallableRuntimeChannels = @('stable', 'beta', 'nightly')
# END GENERATED INSTALLABLE CHANNELS

